  "reason": "The best result so far is config_036 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 accuracy. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, multiprofile over singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l over resnet50, and concat over weighted fusion. The one remaining untested variable within this best-performing family is the aggregation method: we have only tested avgpool (0.715) but not transformer. In RNA-only settings, avgpool outperformed transformer (0.591 vs 0.519 for pca_n2000), but the interaction between transformer aggregation and the stronger multimodal fusion (scvi + ViT-L) is unexplored. As the final experiment, config_038 (same as config_036 but with transformer aggregation) is the most direct exploitation of the best configuration, isolating the aggregation effect in the multimodal regime. If it underperforms, it confirms avgpool is optimal and config_036 stands as the final best; if it surpasses 0.715, we gain a new best. No other untested configuration has a stronger prior probability of exceeding 0.715."
